# This file applies only to a build whose context is the repository root, which
# is the backend image alone; every other service builds from its own directory
# and reads that directory's ignore file, if it has one.
#
# The backend context is the root because the image builds the cqlite reader
# from cqlite-datafusion/ as well as installing the Python app.  Everything is
# excluded and the two directories the image needs are named back in, rather
# than the other way round: cassandra-data/ alone is several gigabytes, and it
# would otherwise be copied to the build on every rebuild.
*
!backend
!cqlite-datafusion

# Local build output, which the image builds for itself.  The Rust target
# directory reaches double figures in gigabytes.
cqlite-datafusion/target
backend/**/__pycache__
